%I A400205 #14 Oct 02 2026 21:40:34
%S A400205 1,1,2,3,4,7,10,13,16,19,22,25,28,31,59,87,146,205,351,497,643,789,
%T A400205 1432,2075,2718,3361,4004,4647,8651,12655,21306,33961,55267,76573,
%U A400205 97879,174452,272331,370210,468089,565968,663847,761726,859605,957484,1055363,1153242,1251121,1349000,1446879
%N A400205 Denominators of semiconvergents of log_2(5).
%C A400205 Here "semiconvergents" includes the principal convergents, as in A206788. The initial term 1 occurs twice, once for the strict lower and once for the strict upper one-sided approximation. All later terms occur once. Put alpha=log_2(5). The lower-side terms are exactly the positive integers r for which {r*alpha} is a strict record minimum relative to {j*alpha}, 1<=j<r. The upper-side terms are exactly those for which {r*alpha} is a strict record maximum relative to the same preceding values. Equivalently, with m_r=floor(r*alpha), the lower and upper terms are the strict record minima and maxima, respectively, of 5^r/2^m_r. These are precisely the equality orders in the natural cycle bounds for A174795. If r>1 is a lower-side term and m=floor(r*alpha), then A174795(r)=binomial(m,r)/m. If r is an upper-side term, then A174795(r)=binomial(m+1,r)/(m+1). Thus the extremal values are rational Catalan numbers. A046104, the denominators of the principal convergents to log_2(5), is a subsequence.
%H A400205 Mike Winkler, <a href="/A400205/b400205.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..200</a>
%H A400205 Mike Winkler, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.22303">Admissible qx+1 Sequences, Semiconvergents, and Rational Catalan Numbers</a>, arXiv:2609.22303 [math.GM], Sep 2026.
%F A400205 Let alpha=[a_0;a_1,a_2,...], Q_(-1)=0, Q_0=1, and Q_(k+1)=a_(k+1)*Q_k+Q_(k-1). Since a_1=3, the sequence starts 1,1,2. For k>=1, append Q_k and then Q_(k-1)+s*Q_k for 1<=s<a_(k+1). These latter terms lie strictly between Q_k and Q_(k+1), so the blocks concatenate in increasing order.
%e A400205 Lower-side terms begin: 1, 4, 7, 10, 13, 16, 19, 22, 25, 28, 87, 146, 789, 1432, 2075, 2718, 3361, 4004.
%e A400205 Upper-side terms begin: 1, 2, 3, 31, 59, 205, 351, 497, 643, 4647, 8651, 21306, 97879, 1936274, 15392313.
%o A400205 (PARI) semidens(q,N) = {localprec(max(100,5*N)); my(c=contfrac(log(q)/log(2),N+2), qm=1, Q=c[2], qn, v=List()); listput(v,1); if(N==1, return(Vec(v))); listput(v,1); if(N==2, return(Vec(v))); for(t=2,c[2]-1, listput(v,t); if(#v==N, return(Vec(v)))); for(k=1,#c-2, if(Q>1, listput(v,Q); if(#v==N, return(Vec(v)))); for(s=1,c[k+2]-1, listput(v,qm+s*Q); if(#v==N, return(Vec(v)))); qn=c[k+2]*Q+qm; qm=Q; Q=qn); Vec(v)}
%Y A400205 Cf. A028508 (continued fraction expansion of log_2(5)), A046104 (denominators of principal convergents to log_2(5)), A174795 (5x+1 admissible-sequence counts), A206788 (the analogous sequence for log_2(3)).
%K A400205 nonn,frac,easy,new
%O A400205 1,3
%A A400205 _Mike Winkler_, Sep 21 2026
